Capture Previous Issues & Fixes

Every significant issue we have previously identified and resolved should become a reusable Skill.

Each Skill should include:

Problem

A clear description of the issue.

Example:

Discovery modules marked as "Skipped"
Data mismatches between dashboards
Broken synchronization
Incorrect score calculations
Missing backend hooks
SSE failures
UI inconsistencies
Root Cause

Explain why the issue occurred.

Examples:

Incorrect API mapping
Missing backend event
Invalid state management
Duplicate calculations
Missing synchronization
Race conditions
Incorrect dependency order
Solution

Document the proven implementation that resolved the issue.

Include:

Code patterns
Architecture improvements
Validation logic
Error handling
Testing strategy
Prevention Checklist

Include a checklist that prevents the same issue from occurring again.

Continuous Knowledge Growth

These Skills should not remain static.

They should continuously evolve as the QGuard Helix platform grows.

For every future interaction, development task, feature implementation, bug fix, architecture improvement, optimization, or enhancement:

Identify reusable knowledge.
Determine whether an existing Skill should be updated.
If the knowledge is new, create a new Skill.
Improve existing Skills with newly learned best practices.
Expand implementation guidelines where appropriate.
Record lessons learned from debugging and production issues.
Update validation checklists and architectural guidance.

This ensures the knowledge base becomes progressively more comprehensive and valuable over time.

